<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-RAM-I2>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-RAM-I2" ;
  triage:title "Ephemeral herdr-wake-pending roster API has zero production callers -- AW-POOL-V7's ephemeral-state requirement is scaffolded but not wired" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr, qa-pr1240-r1 (arch-qa and ruthless-boundary-qa independently, same finding). RosterMemberEphemeralState::herdr_wake_pending and its accessors (LocalServiceRuntime::roster_ephemeral_state at service_runtime.rs:848 and set_roster_herdr_wake_pending at 859) are unused: herdr_queue_wake.rs (the only stated consumer per the doc comment at service_runtime.rs:44-46) contains no call to either method and no reference to wake_pending/WakePending/pending_wake anywhere in the crate. The doc comment asserts a wiring that does not exist yet, which will mislead the next reader into believing the ephemeral-state layer is already load-bearing for Herdr. AW-POOL-V7 explicitly required '(c) ephemeral state mutates in RAM only, on state changes' as part of the retained design; this PR builds the mechanism but does not satisfy that requirement for any real state change. Acceptance: either wire herdr_queue_wake.rs's actual wake-pending bookkeeping through set_roster_herdr_wake_pending/roster_ephemeral_state in this same fix round, or delete the unused public surface until a real caller lands, and soften the doc comment so it doesn't claim current behavior that doesn't exist." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "step2_verdict" ;
  triage:category "requirement-gap" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-06T02:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AWReadinessReview ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-06T01:40:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AW-RAM-I2/unwired-ephemeral-api> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

